> macOS runtime setup

The macOS archive is unsigned and does not bundle Python, Whisper, PyTorch or
model weights. Install the optional runtime manually in a user-owned virtual
environment before enabling the filter.

=> Install the prerequisites

Install Homebrew if it is not already available, then install Python 3.11 and
FFmpeg:

```sh
brew install python@3.11 ffmpeg
```

Create the environment and install the CPU baseline. The PyTorch CPU index is
used deliberately; Apple GPU/MPS support remains an explicit host choice and
is not claimed by this unsigned package:

```sh
runtime_root="$HOME/Library/Application Support/Sythos/OBS-WhisperBleep/runtime-venv"
python3.11 -m venv "$runtime_root"
"$runtime_root/bin/python" -m pip install --upgrade pip
"$runtime_root/bin/python" -m pip install \
  --index-url https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cpu \
  --extra-index-url https://pypi.org/simple \
  -r "$PWD/requirements-cpu.txt"
```

The command above assumes the shell is currently in the installed package's
`share/obs-whisperbleep` directory. If that directory is not convenient, use
the absolute path to the packaged `requirements-cpu.txt`.

=> Tell OBS which Python to use

Launch OBS Studio from a terminal after exporting the interpreter path:

```sh
export OBS_WHISPERBLEEP_PYTHON="$HOME/Library/Application Support/Sythos/OBS-WhisperBleep/runtime-venv/bin/python"
open -a "OBS"
```

Alternatively, configure the same variable in the shell or launcher used to
start OBS. Download and verify a Whisper model through the plugin before
enabling censorship. Model weights are never included in this archive.

The plugin is provided as-is. macOS signing and notarization are not included
because the Apple developer membership, certificates and administrative
requirements are not economically sustainable for this project at its current
stage.
